personate the  not-so-jolly giant thanks to their  somewhat contentious history with each  other  dickie also suggests that this might be  the reason why banner landed directly in  dr. Strange's sanctum sanctorum when he  returned to earth  loki has encountered the master of the  mystic arts before so it's possible that  he may have directed his path from outer  space towards dr. strange knowing he'd  be a quality choice to spearhead the  fight against Thanos if all of this is  true it could mean that the Hulk wasn't  even on the Asgardian refugee ship at  the start of infinity war escaping with  Valkyrie the breakout character of Thor  Ragnarok who is expected to return in  the future MCU film the only problem is  that well it's probably not true at all  if you take Occam's razor - the Loki as  banner theory you'll find there's a much  simpler explanation for all of its  points for starters by the time tano's  shows up on the S guardianship he's  already dealt with Loki before and knows  how he operates he be prepared for and  expecting deceptive tactics like  illusions in shape-shifting second and  probably most importantly banners  struggles with the Hulk make a lot more  sense as banner actually struggling with  the Hulk  rather than Loki working a long con on  the Avengers the Hulk's encounter with  dados marks the first time that the  green Goliath has been so easily  defeated in a fight which would shatter  his confidence and explain why he's so  unwilling to make a return also there  are several scenes in infinity war where  banner attempts to turn into the Hulk  when no one is around to see it that  would only make sense for Loki if he  suddenly had Deadpool levels of  fourth-wall breaking self-awareness  banners arrival at the sanctum sanctorum  is pretty easy to explain away with  magic but probably happened because that  scene is lifted from the original comics  the only difference is that there it's  the Silver Surfer who ruins strangest  staircases  but since he doesn't currently exist in  the MCU banner makes a fitting  substitute as for banners encounter with  Black Widow there actually is some  tension there but it's certainly not the  focus that however is easily explained  by the fact that the romance teased an  age of Ultron wasn't exactly the best  part of that movie some viewers felt  like it came out of  where and didn't really serve either  character well so it makes sense that  the next film might down plan or maybe  Bruce Banner just doesn't prefer blondes  thanks for watching click the looper  icon to subscribe to our YouTube channel  plus check out all this cool stuff we  know you love to  [Music]
 

